  "_commit": {
    "id": "59c39e31f93210197ef1c3a8d7f689d68a091df5",
    "author": "Ossama Edbali <ossedb@gmail.com>",
    "committer": "GitHub <noreply@github.com>",
    "message": "feat: Enable support for ThermoFisher raw instrument file reading (#20)\n\nReplace direct mzR calls throughout the codebase with a new S4-based\n  reader abstraction (`R/raw-file-reader.R`) that decouples the package\n  from any single file-reading backend.\n\n  New S4 class hierarchy:\n  - `MsRawReader` \u2014 virtual base class defining the reader interface\n  - `MzrReader` \u2014 wraps an open mzR connection for standard open formats\n    (.mzML, .mzXML, .CDF)\n  - `RawrrReader` \u2014 wraps a file path for ThermoFisher .raw files via\n    the rawrr package (added to Suggests)\n\n  New generics (all defined in raw-file-reader.R):\n  - `ms_header(reader)` \u2014 returns a normalised scan-header data.frame;\n    for CDF files the BPC/TIC values are computed from raw peaks inside\n    the method, removing the special-case branch that previously lived in\n    `create_bpc_tic()`\n  - `ms_peaks(reader, scans)` \u2014 always returns a list of matrices, even\n    for a single scan, so callers use `[[1]]` consistently\n  - `ms_close(reader)` \u2014 closes the backend connection (no-op for\n    RawrrReader)\n  - `ms_chromatogram(reader, mz, ppm, rt_range)` \u2014 native XIC extraction\n    (RawrrReader delegates to rawrr::readChromatogram(); MzrReader raises\n    an informative error)\n  - `open_raw_reader(path)` \u2014 factory function that dispatches by file\n    extension\n\n  Internal changes:\n  - `R/io-raw-data.R` deleted; its two helpers (`io_get_raw_data`,\n    `io_close_raw_data`) reimplemented in raw-file-reader.R using the new\n    abstraction\n  - All scattered `mzR::header()`, `mzR::peaks()`, `mzR::openMSfile()`,\n    and `mzR::close()` calls in constructors-chromatograms.R,\n    constructors-spectra.R, creators-chromatograms.R, creators-spectra.R,\n    and creators-intensity-map.R replaced with the new generics\n  - `create_chromatogram()` now branches on reader class for XIC: uses\n    `ms_chromatogram()` for RawrrReader and the existing scan-by-scan loop\n    for MzrReader\n  - Guard added in `creators-chromatograms.R` so that empty m",
    "time": 1772643301
  },
